#: ../../../prop_tgt/AUTOGEN_TARGET_DEPENDS.rst:2
msgid "AUTOGEN_TARGET_DEPENDS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/AUTOGEN_TARGET_DEPENDS.rst:4
msgid ""
"Additional target dependencies of the corresponding :ref:`<ORIGIN>_autogen "
"<<ORIGIN>_autogen>` target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/AUTOGEN_TARGET_DEPENDS.rst:9
msgid ""
"If the :ref:`<ORIGIN>_autogen_timestamp_deps "
"<<ORIGIN>_autogen_timestamp_deps>` target is created, additional target "
"dependencies are added to it instead of the :ref:`<ORIGIN>_autogen "
"<<ORIGIN>_autogen>` target.  When using the :ref:`Visual Studio Generators`, "
"the ``moc`` and ``uic`` step may be part of the ``<ORIGIN>`` target itself, "
"in which case the dependencies are added to ``<ORIGIN>``.  See the :manual:"
"`cmake-qt(7)` manual for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/AUTOGEN_TARGET_DEPENDS.rst:18
msgid ""
"Targets which have their :prop_tgt:`AUTOMOC` or :prop_tgt:`AUTOUIC` property "
"``ON`` have a corresponding :ref:`<ORIGIN>_autogen <<ORIGIN>_autogen>`  "
"target which generates ``moc`` and ``uic`` files. As this :ref:"
"`<ORIGIN>_autogen <<ORIGIN>_autogen>` target is created at generate-time, it "
"is not possible to define dependencies of it using e.g. :command:"
"`add_dependencies`.  Instead the ``AUTOGEN_TARGET_DEPENDS`` target property "
"can be set to a :ref:`semicolon-separated list <CMake Language Lists>` of "
"additional dependencies for the :ref:`<ORIGIN>_autogen <<ORIGIN>_autogen>` "
"target. Dependencies can be target names or file names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/AUTOGEN_TARGET_DEPENDS.rst:28
